# Snag Admin Panel Rules

## Security
- NEVER import `SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY` or `SNAG_KEY_ENCRYPTION_SECRET` in `"use client"` files
- NEVER select or return `cursor_api_key_encrypted` or decrypted Cursor keys in API responses
- Use `SAFE_PROJECT_COLUMNS` from `@snag/shared` for all client-facing project queries
- Sensitive mutations go through Route Handlers in `apps/admin/app/api/` with session + role checks
- All Route Handlers must call `writeAuditLog` for create/update/delete/rotate actions
- Never store prompts or screenshot content in audit log metadata

## Auth & roles
- Company reads: Supabase user session + RLS
- Company writes: Route Handler + `canManageProject()` (owner/admin only)
- Platform operations: Route Handler + `isPlatformAdminUser()` + service role client
- Platform pages call `requirePlatformAdmin()` in Server Components

## UI
- Use components from `apps/admin/components/ui/` (shadcn-style)
- Destructive actions (disable project, rotate key) require `AlertDialog` confirmation
- Status badges use `StatusBadge` with protocol statuses: queued, running, finished, error
- Pages need loading/empty states; use Sonner toasts for mutation feedback

## Data
- Reuse types and zod schemas from `@snag/shared` — do not duplicate protocol shapes
- New schema changes must include RLS policies in the same migration file
- Slug validation: `^[a-z0-9-]+$`

## Patterns
- Server Components for layouts and initial data
- Client Components for forms, tables with polling, and interactive dialogs
- TanStack Query for request lists; `refetchInterval: 30000` when status is queued or running
